{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# AI Academic Writing Survey Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyzes the LimeSurvey dataset on AI usage in academic writing among master\'s students.\n",
    "\n",
    "The workflow is designed for the survey structure provided in your export, including:\n",
    "- AI frequency of use\n",
    "- AI tools used\n",
    "- academic tasks supported by AI\n",
    "- AI literacy and attitudes\n",
    "- confidence in research activities\n",
    "- good scientific practice scenarios\n",
    "- open-ended responses\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install required libraries if needed\n",
    "# !pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn openpyxl\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 120\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load the survey dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The script expects a LimeSurvey export in `data/results-survey563129.csv`.\n",
    "If the file is missing, a small example dataset is loaded instead so the notebook remains runnable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_path = os.path.join(\"data\", \"results-survey563129.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(data_path):\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(data_path)\n",
    "    print(f\"Loaded dataset from: {data_path}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    example = {\n",
    "        'BFreq': ['Never', 'About monthly', 'About weekly', 'Daily'],\n",
    "        'BTools[SQ1]': ['Yes', 'No', 'Yes', 'Yes'],\n",
    "        'BTools[SQ2]': ['No', 'Yes', 'No', 'Yes'],\n",
    "        'BUse[SQ1]': ['Yes', 'No', 'Yes', 'Yes'],\n",
    "        'BUse[SQ2]': ['No', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'No'],\n",
    "        'BLiteracy[SQ8]': [3, 4, 2, 5],\n",
    "        'BLiteracy[SQ9]': [2, 3, 4, 5],\n",
    "        'BLiteracy[SQ10]': [4, 3, 3, 4],\n",
    "        'BLiteracy[SQ11]': [2, 5, 4, 4],\n",
    "        'CConf[SQ12]': [2, 3, 4, 5],\n",
    "        'CConf[SQ13]': [2, 2, 3, 4],\n",
    "        'EAtt[SQ27]': [3, 4, 2, 5],\n",
    "        'EAtt[SQ28]': [2, 4, 3, 5],\n",
    "        'EAtt[SQ29]': [3, 5, 4, 4],\n",
    "        'FHardest': ['Selecting relevant literature', 'Structuring the argument', 'Keeping a clear red thread', 'Finding sources'],\n",
    "        'FCLARAExpect': ['Useful if it shows trusted sources', 'Useful if it summarises literature', 'Annoying if it gives vague answers', 'Useful if it keeps context']\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    df = pd.DataFrame(example)\n",
    "    print(\"Dataset not found. Using example data instead. Replace with your actual CSV to run analysis on the real dataset.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df.head())\n",
    "print(f\"Rows: {df.shape[0]} | Columns: {df.shape[1]}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Clean the columns\n",
    "\n",
    "LimeSurvey exports often include long column labels. This step strips the question number and keeps a clean variable name."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def clean_column_name(col):\n",
    "    if '. ' in str(col):\n",
    "        return str(col).split('. ')[0].strip()\n",
    "    return str(col).strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "df.columns = [clean_column_name(c) for c in df.columns]\n",
    "print(df.columns[:10].tolist())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Convert yes/no and multiple-response columns\n",
    "\n",
    "Questions such as `BTools` and `BUse` are multi-response. In practice, they should be treated as binary yes/no variables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tool_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith('BTools')]
",
    "use_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith('BUse')]
",
    "\n",
    "for col in tool_cols + use_cols:\n",
    "    if col in df.columns:\n",
    "        df[col] = df[col].fillna('No').astype(str).str.strip().str.lower().eq('yes').astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Tool columns:', tool_cols[:5])\n",
    "print('Use columns:', use_cols[:5])\n",
    "print(df[tool_cols[:3]].head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Descriptive statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "This section summarizes the sample and explores the main distribution of responses."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('Total respondents:', len(df))\n",
    "\n",
    "freq_col = 'BFreq'\n",
    "if freq_col in df.columns:\n",
    "    freq_table = df[freq_col].value_counts(dropna=False).sort_index()\n",
    "    print('\\nAI use frequency:')\n",
    "    print(freq_table)\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "    sns.countplot(data=df, x=freq_col, order=freq_table.index)\n",
    "    plt.title('Frequency of generative AI use in academic work')\n",
    "    plt.xticks(rotation=20)\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('BFreq column not found in the dataset.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Tool usage summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Shows which platforms students report using for academic work."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tool_usage = df[tool_cols].sum().sort_values(ascending=False) if tool_cols else pd.Series(dtype=int)\n",
    "print('\\nTool usage counts:')\n",
    "print(tool_usage)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not tool_usage.empty:\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "    tool_usage.plot(kind='bar', color='royalblue')\n",
    "    plt.title('AI tools used for academic work')\n",
    "    plt.ylabel('Number of respondents')\n",
    "    plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Academic tasks supported by AI\n",
    "\n",
    "This section summarizes what students use AI for, such as understanding concepts, finding literature, or rewriting text."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "task_usage = df[use_cols].sum().sort_values(ascending=False) if use_cols else pd.Series(dtype=int)\n",
    "print('\\nTask usage counts:')\n",
    "print(task_usage)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not task_usage.empty:\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "    task_usage.plot(kind='bar', color='seagreen')\n",
    "    plt.title('Academic tasks supported by AI tools')\n",
    "    plt.ylabel('Number of respondents')\n",
    "    plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Likert-scale summaries\n",
    "\n",
    "The survey uses several 1–5 Likert items. These are summarized by mean score and visualized as bar charts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def summarize_likert(cols, title):\n",
    "    valid_cols = [c for c in cols if c in df.columns]\n",
    "    if not valid_cols:\n",
    "        print(f'No columns found for {title}.')\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    summary = df[valid_cols].apply(pd.to_numeric, errors='coerce').mean().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    print(f'\\n{title}:')\n",
    "    print(summary)\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "    summary.plot(kind='bar', color='darkorange')\n",
    "    plt.axhline(3, color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=1)\n",
    "    plt.title(title)\n",
    "    plt.ylabel('Mean score (1–5)')\n",
    "    plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "literacy_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith('BLiteracy')]\n",
    "conf_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith('CConf')]\n",
    "att_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith('EAtt')]\n",
    "\n",
    "summarize_likert(literacy_cols, 'AI literacy item means')\n",
    "summarize_likert(conf_cols, 'Research confidence item means')\n",
    "summarize_likert(att_cols, 'Attitude item means')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Correlation analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This heatmap helps identify whether higher AI familiarity or more positive attitudes are associated with higher confidence in research activities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "likert_cols = literacy_cols + conf_cols + att_cols\n",
    "likert_data = df[likert_cols].apply(pd.to_numeric, errors='coerce')\n",
    "likert_data = likert_data.dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "if not likert_data.empty:\n",
    "    corr = likert_data.corr()\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n",
    "    sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', fmt='.2f', vmin=-1, vmax=1)\n",
    "    plt.title('Correlation heatmap of key survey variables')\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No valid numeric data available for the correlation heatmap.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Scientific practice items\n",
    "\n",
    "These items capture whether students understand what constitutes appropriate and inappropriate use of AI in academic practice."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dsgp_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith('DGSP')]
",
    "if dsgp_cols:\n",
    "    print('\\nScientific practice item frequencies:')\n",
    "    for c in dsgp_cols:\n",
    "        print(f'\\n{c}:')\n",
    "        print(df[c].value_counts(dropna=False))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No DFG/scientific practice columns were found.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Open-ended responses\n",
    "\n",
    "Open-ended questions are usually best analyzed thematically. This section extracts and displays the raw answers to help identify recurring themes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('\\nHardest part of academic writing:')\n",
    "for val in df['FHardest'].dropna().head(10):\n",
    "    print('-', val)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nCLARA usefulness / annoyance responses:')\n",
    "for val in df['FCLARAExpect'].dropna().head(10):\n",
    "    print('-', val)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Save cleaned dataset\n",
    "This step exports the cleaned file for future use."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.makedirs('data', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "df.to_csv(os.path.join('data', 'cleaned_survey_data.csv'), index=False)\n",
    "print('Cleaned dataset saved to: data/cleaned_survey_data.csv')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Interpretation guide\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the results in this notebook to answer questions such as:\n",
    "- Which AI tools are most commonly used?\n",
    "- For which academic tasks do students rely on AI most often?\n",
    "- Which research activities generate the lowest confidence?\n",
    "- How do students rate AI literacy and ethics awareness?\n",
    "- What themes emerge from the open-ended responses?\n",
    "- Does the post-test show a meaningful change relative to the pre-test?\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intentionally designed to be reusable for both the original pre-test and any future post-test wave."
   ]
  }
 ],
